{"file":"UX Agent Skills-0.6.0-v2.zip","bytes":1342050,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"ux-agent-skills","displayName":"UX Agent Skills","description":"Audit, spec, and verify production-grade experiences for humans and agents alike.","version":"0.6.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/carlsz/ux-agent-skills","homepage":"https://github.com/carlsz/ux-agent-skills","keywords":["ux","usability","heuristics","design","accessibility","cuj","journeys","agent-skills"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/audit-cuj/SKILL.md","name":"audit-cuj","description":"Verify a stored critical user journey by replaying it step by step against the running app, and report the exact step that broke as a cuj report in .ux/audits. Use for \"verify my CUJs\", \"do the journeys still work\", \"journey regression check\", \"which step broke\".","headings":["Audit CUJ — replay a journey and report the step that broke","Inputs","Workflow","1. Snapshot the repo, then select the journeys — and stop if there are none","2. Validate every selected journey before walking it","3. Establish the mode and reach the app","4. Establish each journey's preconditions — the precondition ladder","5. Replay the steps in order","6. Evaluate `success_criteria` — separately, after the steps","7. Grade, then write one report per run","8. Confirm your footprint","Boundaries","Exit criteria (done when)"],"name_hint":"审查 · cuj"},{"path":"skills/render-report/SKILL.md","name":"render-report","description":"Render existing .ux/audits reports into self-contained, offline HTML pages — findings as cards, the captured screenshots as an interactive walk-through flipbook, plus the roll-up dashboard and an index landing page. Use for \"render the report to HTML\", \"HTML view of the audit\", \"open the audit in a browser\", \"flipbook walkthrough\", \"make a shareable report page\".","headings":["Render report — a self-contained HTML view of an audit","Inputs","Workflow","1. Locate the reports","2. Render each report, and the index","3. Report what was written, and confirm the footprint","Boundaries","Exit criteria (done when)"],"name_hint":"render · 报告"},{"path":"skills/spec-cuj/SKILL.md","name":"spec-cuj","description":"Interview the user one question at a time to author critical user journeys, then store each as its own .ux/cujs file with actor, preconditions, numbered steps and expected outcomes, and regenerate the journey index in the host SPEC.md. Use for \"define a CUJ\", \"author journeys\", \"write our user journeys\", \"ux spec\".","headings":["Spec CUJ — author a critical user journey","Inputs","Workflow","Boundaries","Exit criteria (done when)"],"name_hint":"spec · cuj"},{"path":"skills/usability-audit/SKILL.md","name":"usability-audit","description":"Run an expert heuristic usability evaluation of a host app and write a severity-scored report to .ux/audits. Use for \"usability audit\", \"heuristic evaluation\", \"UX audit\", or \"usability review\".","headings":["Usability Audit","Inputs","Workflow","Boundaries","Exit criteria (done when)"],"name_hint":"usability · 审查"},{"path":"skills/ux-audit/SKILL.md","name":"ux-audit","description":"Suite roll-up — fan out to the default UX auditors (usability, accessibility, cuj) against one target, with web performance available opt-in, normalize all findings into the shared .ux/audits contract, and produce one combined go/no-go roll-up. Use for \"full UX audit\", \"audit everything\", \"ux-audit\".","headings":["UX Audit — suite roll-up","Inputs","Workflow","Boundaries","Exit criteria (done when)"],"name_hint":"ux · 审查"}],"commands":[{"path":"commands/README.md","name":"README","description":"","headings":["Slash commands","Commands here"]},{"path":"commands/cuj-audit.md","name":"cuj-audit","description":"Replay your stored critical user journeys against the running app and report the exact step that broke, as a severity-scored cuj report in .ux/audits. Invokes the cuj-auditor persona via the audit-cuj skill.","headings":["/cuj-audit","Arguments","Behavior","What the modes actually prove","Guarantees"]},{"path":"commands/usability-audit.md","name":"usability-audit","description":"Run an expert heuristic usability audit of a host app and write a severity-scored report to .ux/audits. Invokes the usability-auditor persona via the usability-audit skill.","headings":["/usability-audit","Arguments","Behavior","Guarantees"]},{"path":"commands/ux-audit.md","name":"ux-audit","description":"Run the default UX auditor suite (usability + accessibility + cuj) against one target — web performance is opt-in — normalize into the shared .ux/audits contract, and produce one combined go/no-go roll-up. Invokes the ux-audit skill.","headings":["/ux-audit","Arguments","Behavior","Guarantees"]},{"path":"commands/ux-review.md","name":"ux-review","description":"Render your existing .ux/audits reports into self-contained HTML — findings as cards, screenshots as an interactive walk-through flipbook, the roll-up as a go/no-go dashboard, plus an index landing page. Invokes the render-report skill.","headings":["/ux-review","Arguments","Behavior","Guarantees"]},{"path":"commands/ux-spec.md","name":"ux-spec","description":"Interview you to define your app's critical user journeys, write each to .ux/cujs, and regenerate the journey index in your SPEC.md. Invokes the cuj-author persona via the spec-cuj skill.","headings":["/ux-spec","Arguments","Behavior","What to expect from the interview","Guarantees"]}],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["UX Agent Skills","Commands","Installation","Dependencies","Usability Audits","Critical User Journeys","The roll-up — one target, one verdict","Shared reporting contract","Auditing behind a login wall","Visual walk-throughs and shareable HTML reports","Example — auditing a real app (Sprout)","[sev2] Edit save/cancel is invisible and blur commits silently","Contributing"]},{"path":"evals/README.md","headings":["Evals","Layout","Case format","